[
  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071448",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-72854",
      "knowledge_point_id": "691b9107-a935-5965-b3ac-0f3a193ce9bd",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform One Matrix Into Another",
      "problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $X$ into the matrix $W$, where\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}]?\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the $1$st and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $2$nd row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $2$nd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =W.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{3}",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{3}",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "moderate",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-72854",
        "kp_title": "Identifying the Appropriate Row Operation To Transform One Matrix Into Another",
        "kp_href": null
      },
      "topic_id": 149,
