  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-86587",
      "knowledge_point_id": "19fb3196-439e-5466-b50c-615c492167b4",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Complement of a Set Using a Venn Diagram",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/assets/02dabe7099c201f717885a05842e0cb8543bd01cccf0d6c52147f674cde15dce.png)\n\nLet $U={a,b,c,20,40}$ be the universal set and let $R={b,20,40}.$ What is the complement of $R?$",
      "worked_solution": "The complement of $R,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{R},$ consists of all the elements in $U$ that are not in $R.$ To represent $\\overset{―}{R},$ we will shade in all the area of $U$ that is *outside* of $R,$ as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/assets/79900f22c35570b35cf10664768ecf4460a7953ddf7f91dac1893b3ce81339bf.png)\n\nThe elements in the shaded area are $a$ and $c.$ These are the elements of $U$ that are not in $R.$ Therefore, the complement of $R$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{R}={a,c}.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{20,40}",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{a,b,c}",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{a,c}",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{c,40}",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{a,40}",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "easy",
